<%# Shown on the reminder forms when the senior's calls are not in English.

    Remindly translates its own words; it does not translate the caregiver's.
    The title is free text and reaches the voice exactly as typed, so a senior
    set to Spanish otherwise hears "Take meds" dropped into the middle of a
    Spanish sentence, read by a Spanish voice.

    Translating it automatically was considered and rejected: it would mean
    sending every reminder title to a third-party translator — the same titles
    these forms ask people to keep clinical detail out of — and doing it inside
    the webhook that has to answer before the call can speak. A wrong
    translation of "take 2 of the white ones, not the blue" would then be read
    aloud with total confidence to somebody who cannot check it. %>
<% return if senior.blank? || senior.spoken_language == "en-US" %>
<p class="mt-1 text-xs text-amber-700">
  <%= senior.display_name %>'s calls are spoken in
  <%= senior.spoken_language_label.sub(/\s*\(.*\)/, "") %>, and the title is read
  out exactly as you type it — so write it in that language too.
</p>
